{"name":"Polvo de Oro","hex":"#e8b87f","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oro","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Orokolo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oro"}],"entries":[{"title":"Polvo","blocks":[{"text":"Polvo is an American indie rock band from Chapel Hill, North Carolina, formed in 1990. They are known for their intricate musical style which is characterized by the use of dissonant, layered guitars; off-kilter rhythms, and unorthodox yet melodic song structures. The band has since been described as one of the most accomplished acts within the math rock genre, and their distinctive sound is what set them apart from contemporaries at the time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Polvo_06-27-2010.jpg/330px-Polvo_06-27-2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polvo"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Polvo_06-27-2010.jpg/500px-Polvo_06-27-2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Polvo_06-27-2010.jpg/1280px-Polvo_06-27-2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Polvo_06-27-2010.jpg/500px-Polvo_06-27-2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APolvo_06-27-2010.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}